---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { Aside, Card, CardGrid, LinkCard } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import source from '../../generated/source.json';

const repo = 'https://github.com/atronsa/mezgeb';
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Mezgeb',
    description: 'An open-source double-entry ledger with offline sync and cryptographically signed transactions.',
    template: 'splash',
    pagefind: false,
    hero: {
      title: 'The ledger that keeps its books when the network does not',
      tagline:
        'Mezgeb is an open-source double-entry ledger in Rust on PostgreSQL, with offline payments and cryptographically signed transactions.',
      actions: [
        { text: 'Read the docs', link: '/docs/', icon: 'right-arrow' },
        { text: 'API reference', link: '/api/', variant: 'secondary' },
        { text: 'GitHub', link: repo, icon: 'github', variant: 'minimal' },
      ],
    },
  }}
>
  <Aside type="caution" title="Early development">
    Mezgeb is not production ready yet. Do not use it to hold real money. The
    <a href="/docs/roadmap/">roadmap</a> shows what is built and what comes next.
  </Aside>

  <CardGrid>
    <Card title="Every entry balances" icon="approve-check">
      Double entry is enforced three times: by Rust types, by the posting engine, and by the
      database itself. Posted entries never change; corrections are reversals.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Offline is a first-class case" icon="rocket">
      Funds for offline use sit in escrow. Each offline payment is a signed, hash-chained receipt
      that the ledger settles exactly once, whatever order devices sync in.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Tamper-evident history" icon="seti:lock">
      The journal is hash-chained with signed checkpoints, and every change lands in an
      append-only audit log. Balances are re-proven against the journal.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Safe to retry, safe under load" icon="random">
      Idempotent posting means a retry never charges twice. Row-level locking means the same
      balance cannot be spent twice. Money is integer minor units, never floats.
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>Start reading</h2>
  <CardGrid>
    <LinkCard title="Specification" description="What the ledger guarantees." href="/docs/spec/" />
    <LinkCard title="Invariants" description="Every rule it must never break, and how each is tested." href="/docs/invariants/" />
    <LinkCard title="Offline protocol" description="Vouchers, receipts and settlement." href="/docs/offline/" />
    <LinkCard title="Security" description="Threat model, ASVS self-assessment, and how to report." href="/security/" />
  </CardGrid>

  <p class="source">
    Apache-2.0 licensed. Docs built from
    <a href={`${repo}/tree/${source.linkRef}`}>atronsa/mezgeb @ {source.ref === 'local' ? 'a local checkout' : source.ref}</a>.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .source {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
</style>
